   "id": "ca_mount_thompson_harrington_couloir",
   "area_id": "ca_mount_thompson",
   "name": "Harrington Couloir",
   "grade": "3rd AI2 Mod. Snow",
   "discipline": "ice",
   "overview": "Moderate snow and ice climb. Counting from the left while walking in, take the third obvious couloir; it tops out at around 50 degrees. From the top, walk north about 10 minutes over the plateau to a 3rd class scramble of 20' to the summit.",
   "description": null,
   "approach": "From the South Lake parking area take the Bishop Pass trail, fork right onto the Treasure Lakes trail, then leave the trail and climb west over a rock ridge. Beyond it lies the basin below the peak's north side; follow its moraine up to the foot of the face. The couloir is the third of four on the north face, counting Knudtson, Smrz, Harrington and Moynier from the left.",
