   "grade": "5.11",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": null,
   "description": null,
   "approach": "From North Lake, take the trail toward Lamarck Col to Upper Lamarck Lake, then leave the col trail at the foot of the lake. Cross the stream and climb the hill to the shoulder above the lake, staying high because the lake is cliffed out below. Aim for the talus field beneath the wall, which holds a splitter offwidth in its center.",
   "descent_text": "There are no bolted anchors or bail points on the route, so the way off is up and over. From the top, follow the ridge toward the summit of Lamarck, then descend easily toward Lamarck Col and join the col trail in the neighbouring basin. This loop avoids the approach side, where early-season snow can make the lower slope dangerous, so parties carry their gear with them rather than leaving it at the base.",
